def level5():
    lvl = f"""
    Our client's network was infected with this implant that wiped
    out everything on the disks. It seems to be written in golang.
    I had just finished reading the new 
    "Memory Forensics Techniques for Automated Detection and Analysis of Go Malware"
    from Hala Ali, Andrew Case and Irfan Ahmed 
    (https://dfrws.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/DFRWS_USA_2026_Camera_Ready_Paper_19.pdf)
    when i got the call. Got my trusty cold air spray and started spraying every memory
    chip i could find. Since your username is hacker@ maybe you can help me out make sense of 
    the capture {gofiguredataset}?

    for this level, you don't have to get into a heap of trouble to get there.
    """
    print(lvl)
    msgsum = "181102929716d842863c373ee1c6c387"
    userinp = input(">").strip().strip('\n')
    maybe = hashlib.md5(userinp.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()
    check(maybe==msgsum)

